      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Williams%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits just an hour south of the Grand Canyon and is called the “Gateway to the Grand Canyon.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.williamsaz.gov/visitors"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Williams lies on Historic Route 66 and was the last city on the highway to be bypassed by Interstate 40.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Williams%2C_Arizona"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The southern terminus of the Grand Canyon Railway is in Williams, where the historic downtown station still operates.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
